.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.jsonl
sessions/

# Documents the preview pane serves. They are conversation output, sometimes private, and
# regenerable only by re-running the assistant, so they are never committed.
previews/
node_modules/
tests/output_*.html

# Scratch workspace tools/capture.py runs its scenarios in. It is what the captured session reads,
# writes and edits, so it is conversation output and never committed.
data-samples/capture-workspace/

# Local third-party checkouts that this repository path-depends on but cannot publish: the
# RealtimeSTT fork behind the `audio`/`voice` extra and the OmniVoice source. A path dependency on a fork
# that lives on no registry cannot be installed by anyone who cloned this repository, so the directory is
# local-only by decision (audit PK-01) and `pyproject.toml` says so next to the dependency. A fresh clone
# gets the default engine, Phonon, from `uv sync` alone; the extra needs the fork placed here by hand.
experiments/

# Voice validation artifacts
voice-validation/

# TTS audition renders from tools/phonon_probe.py. Regenerable, and they carry the text we
# feed the engine, so they stay local.
voice-samples/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
graft/

# setuptools build artifact
pi_chat.egg-info/

# Profile password hashes and local overrides. Credentials that gate two private chats must never be
# committed. There is no committed template file any more: `docs/configuration.md` lists every name with its
# default, and `python -m pi_chat.auth --account b` writes the one value you actually have to set. The
# `.env.*` pattern is here so a future `env.backup` cannot be committed by accident either.
.env
.env.*

# Sweep 2 (2026-11-17, RH-03/RH-04): these hold personal audio and derived local state.
# They were untracked but not ignored, so any `git add -A` would have committed real voice
# recordings. Ignore first, decide retention separately.
voices/
voice-clone-samples/
voice-debug-audio/
screenshots/
.pytest_cache/

# Sweep 2 follow-up (2026-11-17): `example_files/` held the preview pane's fixtures, and they were not
# fixtures: one was a household member's profile text printed to PDF, one a utility bill remittance stub with
# a name and address on it, one local model-launch flags. All three stayed on disk for anyone who wants them;
# `tools/screenshot_ui.mjs` now generates the bytes its stages need, so nothing here is load-bearing any more.
# They were tracked on three branch tips until that commit, and the audit note that names them is local only.
example_files/

# Personal literals for `tools/scrub_captures.py`: `literal = replacement` pairs naming this machine and the
# people who use it. Committing this file would publish the exact strings the scrubber exists to remove, so it
# is read from here or from $PI_CHAT_SCRUB_LITERALS and never from the repository.
.scrub-literals

# Windows alternate-data-stream leftovers. The names contain `:`, which NTFS cannot hold,
# so they made every index operation need `-c core.protectNTFS=false` (see 1e0ad62).
*.Zone.Identifier

# RealtimeSTT's own module logger writes `realtimesst.log` into the process working directory the first time
# the package is imported, so every voice run drops a ~90 KB log at the repo root. The path is the library's
# choice, not ours, and pi-chat does not configure it, so the honest fix is to ignore it rather than to
# pretend the file is meaningful state.
realtimesst.log

# The quarterly audit registry: dated finding rows and fix writeups. Kept in the working tree because it is
# the memory of what was found, and never committed because it describes real documents and real people on
# this machine, in more detail than a public repository should carry. AGENTS.md says where it lives.
docs/audit/
